---
import research from '../platform-research.json';
import '../report.css';
import '../platform-context.css';
import '../research.css';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'')+'/';
const citations=keys=>keys.map(key=>research.sources[key]);
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="LinkedIn ranking changes from 2019 to 2026, Instagram and search evidence, and their implications for Riad Meddeb’s communication strategy."/><title>Platform research · Riad Meddeb Linkedin analysis</title><link rel="preload" href={base+'fonts/newsreader.woff2'} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin/><link rel="preload" href={base+'fonts/instrument-sans.woff2'} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin/></head><body>
<header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href={base} aria-label="Back to Riad Meddeb Linkedin analysis"><span class="report-brand" aria-hidden="true">in</span></a><a class="research-back" href={base}>Back to the report</a></header>
<main class="research-page">
<h1>Platform research and proposed changes</h1>
<p class="research-date">Reviewed {research.reviewed}</p>
<p class="research-lead">LinkedIn’s 2026 ranking tests report higher engagement from professional matching and interaction histories. Its product team also reports fewer views of content classified as low quality. The evidence below separates controlled test results, reported trends and proposed changes to the communication strategy.</p>
<p class="research-scope">This review uses LinkedIn’s engineering and product publications, a first-hand interview with its leaders, and Meta, Google and Microsoft documentation. The history below records published changes to parts of the system; it is not a complete ranking formula. Instagram, website analytics and partner outcomes are not included in the LinkedIn archive.</p>
<section aria-labelledby="history-title"><h2 id="history-title">How LinkedIn’s ranking has developed</h2><div class="ranking-history">{research.history.map(row=><article><div class="history-year">{row.year}</div><div><h3>{row.title}</h3><p>{row.finding}</p><p class="research-implication">{row.implication}</p><p class="platform-reference">{citations(row.sources).map((source,i)=><>{i>0?' · ':''}<a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a></>)}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="implications-title"><h2 id="implications-title">What this means for the report</h2><div class="research-grid">{research.principles.map(row=><article><h3>{row.title}</h3><p>{row.text}</p>{row.sources.length>0&&<p class="platform-reference">{citations(row.sources).map((source,i)=><>{i>0?' · ':''}<a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a></>)}</p>}</article>)}</div><p class="research-scope">The reviewed primary sources do not establish universal organic ranking multipliers, a fixed first-hour rule or a blanket external-link penalty. They do not justify promising more reach solely from changing format or asking for tags.</p></section>
<section id="channels" aria-labelledby="channels-title"><h2 id="channels-title">Instagram, the UNDP website and AI search</h2>{research.channels.map(row=><article class="channel-research"><h3>{row.title}</h3><p>{row.text}</p><p class="research-implication">{row.application}</p><p class="platform-reference">{citations(row.sources).map((source,i)=><>{i>0?' · ':''}<a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a></>)}</p></article>)}</section>
<section aria-labelledby="assessment-title"><h2 id="assessment-title">Assessment of the proposed changes</h2><div class="proposal-assessment">{research.assessment.map(row=><article><div><h3>{row.suggestion}</h3><p class="assessment-decision">{row.decision}</p></div><p>{row.reason}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="measurement-title"><h2 id="measurement-title">Evaluate attention, relevance and follow-up separately</h2><div class="research-grid">{research.evaluation.map(row=><article><h3>{row.title}</h3><p>{row.text}</p></article>)}</div><p class="research-return"><a href={base+'#conclusion'}>Read the proposed changes in the report</a></p></section>
</main></body></html>
